[[File:Jug of sunfire wine detail.png|130px|left]]
A '''jug of sunfire wine''' is an item created by using two [[sunfire splinters]] on a [[jug of wine]] whilst having a [[pestle and mortar]] in the inventory. Sunfire splinters '''cannot''' be added to a [[jug of blessed wine]]; it must be added to an unblessed jug of wine.

It is used in the process of sacrificing [[blessed bone shards]] at the [[libation bowl]], where one jug can sacrifice 400 shards; players will also need 2 [[Prayer points]] for each sacrifice.

When blessed at the [[exposed altar]] found south of [[the Teomat]], the wine becomes a [[jug of blessed sunfire wine]] (which cannot be banked). This can be used at the libation bowl, in place of a regular jug of blessed wine, to increase the [[Prayer]] experience gained per blessed bone shard from 5 to 6, equivalent to an increase of 400 Prayer experience per wine used.

When buying the sunfire splinters on the [[Grand Exchange]], this results in a cost of {{Coins|2*{{GEP|Sunfire splinters}}/400}} gp per Prayer experience.

